       "text": "ANGLE ID: L1-O01\nSTATUS: Copy complete\nCORE ARGUMENT: October's 83 expired Monroe listings mostly cut their price and still sat for about six months; the pattern points to first-price errors, not a lack of buyers.\nAUDIENCE: Monroe homeowners planning to list; owners whose listing expired\nTAKEAWAY: Price for the competition on day one. Late cuts rarely rescue a listing.\nFORMAT: Ledger article, ~550 words · Effort: Moderate\nSOURCES:\n• Pocono MLS / Flexmls, Monroe County residential, October 1–31, 2026 (pulled Nov 16, 2026). Actives = on market as of the pull. One record with an apparent price error excluded (206 closings).\n• PMAR Monthly Indicators, October 2026 (Monroe County, all residential; ShowingTime, current as of Nov 9, 2026)\nBEFORE POSTING:\n• 'Expired' = listing agreement ended in October without a sale. Withdrawn and canceled listings weren't in the pull, so 83 undercounts listings that left the market unsold.\n• Don't name, address or describe any individual expired listing."
