       "text": "ANGLE ID: BL1-O37\nSTATUS: Copy complete\nCORE ARGUMENT: Selling can work this winter if price fits today's competition; prices are up but activity slowed and the market splits by speed and price range.\nAUDIENCE: Monroe homeowners searching whether to sell now\nTAKEAWAY: Price for current competition, plan the first two weeks, and don't wait on rates.\nFORMAT: SEO/AEO article, ~1,050 words · Effort: Moderate\nSOURCES:\n• PMAR Monthly Indicators, October 2026 (Monroe County, all residential; ShowingTime, current as of Nov 9, 2026)\n• Pocono MLS / Flexmls, Monroe County residential, October 1–31, 2026 (pulled Nov 16, 2026). Actives = on market as of the pull. One record with an apparent price error excluded (206 closings).\n• Flexmls Market Summary, Pocono MLS-wide residential (no county filter), pulled Nov 16, 2026\n• Freddie Mac PMMS, Nov 12, 2026: 30-yr 7.11% (Nov 5: 7.18%) — https://www.freddiemac.com/pmms\nBEFORE POSTING:\n• Overlap: this article pulls together this week's numbers (Ledger posts, reels). Its job is answering the search question, so its sections are written fresh, not pasted from the Ledger.\n• get.realtor: confirm the blog editor supports tables. If not, convert the table to a bulleted list."
