       "text": "ANGLE ID: L3-O02\nSTATUS: Copy complete\nCORE ARGUMENT: October's 9.4% median jump was driven largely by which homes sold, with far fewer lower-priced sales; it overstates what a typical house gained.\nAUDIENCE: Monroe homeowners, sellers, local media readers\nTAKEAWAY: Don't add 9.4% to your home's value. Year-to-date (+7.6%) and your actual competition are better guides.\nFORMAT: Ledger article, ~550 words · Effort: Moderate\nSOURCES:\n• PMAR Monthly Indicators, October 2026 (Monroe County, all residential; ShowingTime, current as of Nov 9, 2026)\n• Flexmls Market Summary, Pocono MLS-wide residential (no county filter), pulled Nov 16, 2026\nBEFORE POSTING:\n• Price-band sales counts come from the MLS-wide CSV (no county filter). They're labeled 'Pocono MLS-wide' in the article.\n• Don't put a number on the mix effect. The data can't isolate it.\n• Overlap: last week's YouTube 1 covered stats literacy in general. This post is only about October's median and why it rose."
