       "label": "Brief",
       "kind": "text",
       "text": "ANGLE ID: YT1-O10\nSTATUS: Copy complete · needs filming\nCORE ARGUMENT: A listing that's sitting has three options (reduce, refresh and relist, or withdraw until spring), and the right one depends on whether buyers are seeing it, seeing it and passing, or giving the same feedback.\nAUDIENCE: Owners with active Monroe listings past 30–60 days\nTAKEAWAY: Diagnose first (seen? offers? feedback?), then make one meaningful move. Waiting only works if you come back different.\nFORMAT: Talking head + graphics, 16:9, ~5.5 min (~800 words) · Effort: Moderate\nSOURCES:\n• Pocono MLS / Flexmls, Monroe County residential, October 1–31, 2026 (pulled Nov 16, 2026). Actives = on market as of the pull. One record with an apparent price error excluded (206 closings).\n• PMAR Monthly Indicators, October 2026 (Monroe County, all residential; ShowingTime, current as of Nov 9, 2026)\n• Hypothetical carrying cost $2,700/mo (labeled).\nBEFORE POSTING:\n• Overlap check: Ledger 1 diagnoses the 83 expireds; TT4 is the after-expiration checklist. This video is the decision guide for owners whose listing is still active.\n• No criticism of other agents or brokerages."
