       "text": "Q: Should I get a radon test when buying a house in Pennsylvania?\nA: Yes. Pennsylvania's DEP estimates about 40% of homes in the state have radon above the EPA action level. Testing is inexpensive and usually done during the inspection period.\n\nQ: Does Pennsylvania test private well water?\nA: No. Pennsylvania's DEP doesn't regulate private wells. Buyers should have the water tested by a DEP-accredited lab.\n\nQ: Do I need a separate septic inspection in the Poconos?\nA: If the home is on an on-lot septic system, yes. It's a separate inspection from the general home inspection.\n\nQ: How old are most homes for sale in Monroe County, PA?\nA: Among October 2026 sales, the median year built was 1989, and only 10 of 206 homes were built in 2010 or later."
