       "text": "ANGLE ID: L4-O03\nSTATUS: Copy complete\nCORE ARGUMENT: Monroe's market isn't one market. Homes over $500K have about 5.9 months of supply and the longest selling times; homes under $250K move fastest.\nAUDIENCE: Sellers in each price range; move-up buyers\nTAKEAWAY: Know your price range's speed before you set expectations. Over $500K, plan for competition and time.\nFORMAT: Ledger article, ~575 words · Effort: Moderate\nSOURCES:\n• Pocono MLS / Flexmls, Monroe County residential, October 1–31, 2026 (pulled Nov 16, 2026). Actives = on market as of the pull. One record with an apparent price error excluded (206 closings).\nBEFORE POSTING:\n• Months of supply here = active listings (Nov 16) ÷ October closings in that range. It's a single-month snapshot, not PMAR's official months-of-supply figure.\n• Actives and expireds are grouped by list price; closings by sale price."
