      {
       "label": "SEO",
       "kind": "text",
       "text": "SEO TITLE (54 chars): Monroe County Homes by Price Range: Who's Selling Fast\nMETA DESCRIPTION (139 chars): Monroe County homes over $500K have about 5.9 months of supply; under $250K about 3.4. What each price range means for sellers this winter.\nSLUG: /pocono-ledger-monroe-price-ranges-november-2026\nPRIMARY KEYWORD: Monroe County housing market by price range\nPUBLISH: Friday, November 20, 2026\nFEATURED IMAGE: Two contrasting Pocono homes side by side: a modest ranch and a larger lakeside or mountain home, from public roads.\nALT TEXT: A modest ranch home and a larger mountain home in the Poconos.\nSERIES: The Pocono Ledger · Week of Nov 16, 2026"
      },
      {
       "label": "Article",
       "kind": "text",
       "text": "# Two Speeds in One County: Where Monroe Homes Are Moving and Where They're Sitting\n\nBy Alexa Sanchez, REALTOR® · PA License No. RS326383 · Smart Way America Realty · 528 Seven Bridges Rd, Suite 108, East Stroudsburg, PA 18301 · (570) 688-8147 · Alexa@alexasanchez.net\nThe Pocono Ledger · Friday, November 20, 2026\n\n**The number:** Homes listed at $500,000 or more in Monroe County have about 5.9 months of supply. Homes under $250,000 have about 3.4.\n\nCountywide numbers blend those together. If you're selling, your price range matters more than the county average.\n\n## What happened\n\nI compared Monroe County's active listings as of November 16 with October's sales and expired listings, by price range, using Pocono MLS data.\n\n| Price range | For sale now | Sold in Oct | Expired in Oct | Months of supply* | Median days on market (sold) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Under $250K | 130 | 38 | 12 | ~3.4 | 26 |\n| $250K–$399K | 392 | 90 | 41 | ~4.4 | 36 |\n| $400K–$499K | 155 | 42 | 13 | ~3.7 | 38.5 |\n| $500K+ | 213 | 36 | 17 | ~5.9 | 43 |\n\n*Active listings divided by one month of sales. It's a snapshot, not an official figure.\n\n## What it means\n\nIt isn't a straight line where everything gets slower as price goes up. The $400,000–$499,999 range is moving faster than the $250,000–$399,999 range, which has the most competition in raw numbers: 392 homes for sale.\n\nThe top of the market is where supply is building fastest. Across the whole Pocono MLS, new listings priced $500,000 and up rose from 82 last October to 122 this October. In Monroe, there were 17 expired $500,000+ listings in October for every 36 that sold.\n\nBelow $250,000, homes sell quickly, but there are fewer of them, and they're often older or need work.\n\n## Who it affects\n\n- **$500,000+ sellers:** Expect more competition and more time. Pricing and presentation have to be sharper than in any other range.\n- **$250,000–$399,999 sellers:** The busiest part of the market. You'll be compared with lots of similar homes, so condition and photos decide who gets the showing.\n- **Under-$250,000 sellers:** Buyers move fast, but they're inspecting carefully and often financing with tight budgets.\n- **Move-up buyers:** Selling a lower-priced home and buying above $500,000 is a favorable combination right now. You're selling where it's fast and buying where buyers have room.\n\n## What to do\n\n1. **Find your range's speed** before setting a timeline or price.\n2. **Above $500,000,** plan your launch like it matters most, because it does: price, photos and first-week showings.\n3. **If you're moving up,** talk through sequencing (sell first, buy first, or contingent) before you list.\n\n## Misconception to correct\n\n\"The market is slow.\" Some of it is. Some of it is moving in under a month. It depends on your price.\n\n---\n\n**Source notes.** Pocono MLS / Flexmls, Monroe County residential: active listings as of November 16, 2026 (890, grouped by current list price); closings October 1–31, 2026 (206, by sale price; one record with an apparent price error excluded); expired listings October 1–31, 2026 (83, by list price). Pocono MLS-wide $500,000+ new listings: Flexmls Market Summary, all areas. Information deemed reliable but not guaranteed."
      }
