       "text": "Selling or buying in Monroe County? Budget for the realty transfer tax.\n\nIn most of Monroe County, the realty transfer tax on a deed is 2% of the price: 1% to Pennsylvania and 1% local. On a $350,000 sale, that's $7,000 total.\n\nWho pays? Pennsylvania law holds both buyer and seller responsible for the tax. In practice, your sales agreement decides how it's split. Splitting it evenly is common, but contracts vary, so read yours before you sign.\n\nSome transfers between family members are exempt. Ask your attorney or settlement company about your situation.\n\nQuestions about your costs to sell in Stroudsburg, East Stroudsburg or anywhere in the Poconos? Tap Call.\n\nAlexa Sanchez · PA License No. RS326383 · Smart Way America Realty · 528 Seven Bridges Rd, Suite 108, East Stroudsburg, PA 18301"
